maluos-office-setup (0.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The first sign-in can be checked and repaired: scripts/admin-login.py
    (--check: the administrator's member, the stored password against it,
    the sign-in throttle, the session cookie for the office's scheme, a real
    sign-in on the office; --reset: a new generated password, stored
    root-only, failed attempts cleared) and `maluctl office-setup admin
    [check|reset]`. The skill runs the check before handing the sign-in over
    and when the operator reports that it fails; verify.sh runs it too.
  * `claude` is found after the setup: `maluctl office-setup` adds
    ~/.local/bin to ~/.bashrc when the shell does not search it and says how
    to use it in the open shell; /etc/profile.d/maluos-local-bin.sh adds it
    for login shells. Before, `claude` typed after the setup answered
    "command not found" until the next login.
  * Local changes to the vendored plugin (to be carried to its repository):
    scripts/admin-login.py, scripts/verify.sh, skills/office-setup/SKILL.md,
    skills/office-check/SKILL.md, the troubleshooting reference.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0000

maluos-office-setup (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First version: the maluos-office-setup Claude Code plugin (skills
    office-setup, office-providers, office-check; the scripts preflight.py,
    configure-kernel.py, provision.sh, verify.sh, hosts-proxy.sh,
    proxy-config.sh, set-provider-key.sh, vm-guest.sh) vendored under
    /usr/share/maluos/claude-plugins with a local marketplace, the sudoers
    rule for its scripts, the launcher, and `maluctl office-setup`
    (run|check|status|providers). In seeds/business-os.seed, so every
    server image that carries the kernel carries the plugin that
    configures it (the handbook's 23-office-setup-package.md, phase 2).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
